      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "It looks like there used to be a mod for this.. https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=yEobsmqpvlc\n\nIt's two lines of code to implement a 360 camera in unity but VRChat doesn't allow scripts on avatars, even locally.  It seems like tools such as VRClens would be unable to implement this.\n\nThe developers have managed to suppress the most creative community members.\n\nUpdate... I found someone who has implemented 360cam using a shader VoxK-360cam:  https://vrchat.com/home/launch?worldId=wrld_acaa99fb-02a5-4b25-8190-6ff6003ac40b",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2019-10-19T20:51:25.022Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Would it ever be possible to add another camera in the camera menu such as a 360 camera for content recording? Say; a user would like to make a content video for 360 footage in something such as YouTube? I certainly see a great degree of use which may also encourage even more people to adopt VR as a media  median.",
